      - For custom envs: follow each repo's README.

  implementation_strategy: |
    Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)
      - Set up project structure, virtual environment, install core dependencies.
      - Implement utility modules: replay buffer, trajectory collector, state save/restore wrapper for MuJoCo.
      - Implement RND module (target network, predictor network, update rule).
      - Write unit tests for these components.

    Phase 2: Mask Network (Week 2-3)
      - Implement MaskNet architecture and training loop (PPO-based) in mask_net.py.
      - Implement importance extraction and fidelity score computation.
      - Test on a simple environment (CartPole) with a pre-trained PPO agent: verify that masking non-critical steps does not drop performance, and that importance scores correlate with action Q-values.
      - Compare training time against a naive StateMask reimplementation to confirm efficiency gain.

    Phase 3: RICE Refiner (Week 3-4)
      - Implement the full RICE pipeline in rice_refiner.py:
          a. Critical state identification from stored trajectories.
          b. Mixed initial distribution sampling.
          c. Integration of RND exploration bonus into PPO training loop.
      - Test on Hopper-v3: train a target PPO agent, run RICE refinement, observe performance improvement over baseline PPO fine-tune.

    Phase 4: Baselines (Week 4-5)
      - Implement baseline methods in baselines.py:
          - PPO fine-tuning (simply continue training).
          - JSRL (integrate open-source code or reimplement core idea).
          - SIL (add SIL loss to PPO update).
          - Random explanation (shuffle importance scores).
      - For StateMask-R, use the official StateMask code to generate explanations, then feed into our refiner.
      - For Integrated Gradients / AIRS, implement or adapt existing libraries to produce state importance scores.

    Phase 5: Additional Environments (Week 5-6)
      - Integrate sparse reward variants for MuJoCo (modify reward functions).
      - Integrate Selfish Mining environment: write wrapper to match our interface.
      - Integrate CAGE Challenge 2: adapt the champion blue agent code.
      - Integrate MetaDrive autonomous driving: write wrapper for "Macro-v1".
      - Integrate MalConv malware mutation: write wrapper, ensure action space matches Table 2.
      - For each, train a target PPO agent and verify basic functionality.

    Phase 6: Evaluation Suite (Week 6-7)
      - Implement evaluate.py to compute:
          - Average episode return (with confidence intervals).
          - Fidelity scores.
          - Training time measurements.
      - Implement run_all_experiments.py to orchestrate the full set of experiments with proper seeding and logging.
      - Write plotting scripts to reproduce figures (learning curves, sensitivity heatmaps, fidelity bar charts).

    Phase 7: Reproduction & Tuning (Week 7-8)
      - Run all experiments on available hardware (at least 1 GPU, ideally multiple).
      - Compare results against paper's reported numbers (Tables 1,4,5,6,7; Figures 5-15).
      - Tune hyperparameters if necessary to match paper's results (use Table 3 as starting point).
      - Document any discrepancies and possible reasons (e.g., different PyTorch versions, environment stochasticity).

    Phase 8: Documentation & Packaging (Week 8)
      - Write README.md with:
          - Overview of RICE.
          - Installation instructions.
          - Usage examples (train mask, refine agent, evaluate).
          - Reproduction instructions (how to run all experiments).
          - Link to paper and citation.
      - Finalize requirements.txt with exact versions used.
      - Clean up code, add docstrings, ensure reproducibility.

    Handling Missing Details:
      - If exact network architectures for mask network in non-MuJoCo domains are not specified, use the same architecture as the target agent's policy network.
      - For state restoration in environments without set_state(), implement an action-replay approach: store the sequence of actions from episode start to critical state, then replay them to reach the same state (may be stochastic; use deterministic environments or average).
      - The paper mentions "top-K critical states" but not exact K; we will use K = 10 per episode or top 10% of states, and make it configurable.
      - For the mask network intrinsic reward coefficient α, the paper has conflicting values (0.01 in text, 0.0001 in Table 3). We will default to 0.0001 as per Table 3 and allow override.
      - The RND networks: use MLP with 2 hidden layers of 64 units, output dimension 128 (common in literature).
